course: dictionary
lesson: 6748
title: Only: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Only is a small word with many jobs. Most of the time it means just, or no more than: «Only 3 are left» means there are just three. Read the words around it, and the meaning often shows itself.
explain: Only can also mean nobody or nothing else. «Only Sam knew» means Sam was the one person who knew. The words around only tell you which person or thing is picked out.
explain: Only can even mean but in casual talk. «I'd come, only I'm busy» means I'd come, but I'm busy. Dictionaries mark this as informal, so save it for chatting, not for school writing.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If only means just, then «only half» means just half, which makes sense in a maths problem. If your meaning makes no sense, try another.
fact: Only means no more than, or just one: «Only 3 are left.»
fact: Only can mean nobody or nothing else: «Only Sam knew.»
fact: An only child has no brothers or sisters.
fact: «If only» shows a wish: «If only it would stop raining.»
fact: In casual talk, only can mean «but»: «I'd come, only I'm busy.»
exercise: «Only 3 are left in the tin.» What does only mean here? | Only in the tin, not in the box | *Just 3, no more than 3 | Nobody else is in the tin | A wish for more biscuits
exercise: «Only Sam knew the answer.» What does only show? | Sam knew many answers | Sam forgot the answer | *Sam was the one person who knew | Sam was the last to leave
exercise: Find the words that show a wish in «If only it would stop raining». | it | *If only | it would stop | raining
test: «Super glue can glue your eyelids, so only an adult uses it.» What does only mean here? | Just | *Nobody else | Very slowly | Until
test: Ella says, «I'd come, only I'm busy.» What does only mean here? | Nobody else | *But | Wishing | Just
exam: «In a fair test you change only one thing and keep everything else the same.» What does only mean here? | Nobody else | But | A wish | *Just one, no more than one
